# Every mesher, step 4 (2026-11-10): SALOME's structured hexahedra picked under Mesh settings mesh a box through the app
# (headless SALOME, then ideasUnvToFoam); Gmsh's 3-D algorithm is chosen there and saved.
budget p95 60 max 400
shell python3 "$QC_TESTS/tools/gen_named_box.py" $SB/ws/box.stl
open $SB/ws/cavity
click nav:mesh
wait-until page Mesh
click text:STL mesher
wait 5
click stl-path
enter $SB/ws/box.stl
wait 10
click stl-next
wait 3
click stl-next
wait 5
click stl-name-kinds
wait 3
click stl-next
wait 5
click stl-mesher
wait 3
click text:SALOME · Structured hex (i,j,k): block-like parts
wait 5
assert text Structured hexahedra: edges divided at the target size
assert text makes no prism layers
click stl-next
wait 5
click stl-gen
wait-until job running timeout 20
wait-until job finished timeout 600
assert log log.salome structured hexahedra (i,j,k)
assert log log.checkMesh Mesh OK.
assert log log.checkMesh hexahedra
screenshot $OUT/1_hexa.png
click stl-step#3
wait 5
click stl-mesher
wait 3
click text:SALOME · Tetrahedral: Gmsh
wait 5
assert text Gmsh 3-D algorithm
click stl-gmsh-algo#2
wait 3
assert log mesher/mesher.ini gmsh_algorithm = hxt
assert log mesher/mesher.ini mesher = sgmsh
screenshot $OUT/2_gmsh.png
